{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Please, adoni.</b> Secular, and it takes kamatz because it is the end of a verse. R. Samuel the Spaniard, the Nagid, of blessed memory, said that אל נא is from the root הואל. In my opinion it is like לא, for when they said to him, 'Flee to the mountain,' he replied, 'No,' my masters."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:07.999284871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}